<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title><%= title %> - WordPress Schema Generator</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css">
  <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/img/favicon.svg">
  <meta name="csrf-token" content="<%= typeof csrfToken !== 'undefined' ? csrfToken : '' %>">
  <script src="/js/auth.js"></script>
</head>
<body>
  <header class="header">
    <div class="container">
      <h1 class="logo"><img src="/img/favicon.svg" class="logo-mark" alt="">Schema Generator</h1>
      <nav class="nav">
        <% if (typeof currentUser !== 'undefined' && currentUser) { %>
        <form method="post" action="/logout" class="logout-form">
          <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>">
          <span><%= currentUser %></span>
          <button class="btn btn-secondary" type="submit">Sign out</button>
        </form>
        <% } %>
        <button class="btn btn-secondary" id="open-help">Help</button>
        <button class="theme-toggle" id="theme-toggle" title="Toggle dark mode">
          <span class="icon">🌙</span>
          <span class="label">Dark</span>
        </button>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </header>

  <dialog id="help-dialog" class="site-dialog">
    <div style="padding:1.5rem">
      <div class="dialog-heading">
        <div><span class="eyebrow">GUIDE</span><h2>How this works</h2></div>
        <button type="button" class="icon-button" id="close-help">×</button>
      </div>

      <h3>1. Connect a site</h3>
      <p>Click <strong>Add site</strong>. Enter the WordPress URL and an Application Password (WordPress → Users → Profile → Application Passwords). Choose an integration:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Workspace Connector</strong> (recommended for Rank Math) — download the plugin from the toolbar, install and activate it on the site, then select this integration. It's what makes replace/remove of existing schema reversible.</li>
        <li><strong>Direct REST metadata</strong> — no plugin needed. Point at any REST-exposed post-meta field; your theme renders it as JSON-LD.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="muted">Optionally set a <strong>default schema image</strong> in site settings — used only on pages that don't have their own image.</p>

      <h3>2. Save your AI key</h3>
      <p>Click <strong>AI Settings</strong> and paste your OpenAI or Gemini API key. Schema generation always uses AI — there is no non-AI fallback.</p>

      <h3>3. Work through the wizard</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Pages</strong> — click <strong>Crawl site</strong> to discover pages (sitemap, WordPress discovery, or pasted URLs), then check which ones to work with.</li>
        <li><strong>Action</strong> — choose <strong>Create new schema</strong> (AI generates JSON-LD) or <strong>Delete existing schema</strong> (removes app-published schema), for the pages you selected.</li>
        <li><strong>Review</strong> — for Create, click Generate; for Delete, removal is already previewed. Either way, open <strong>Review</strong> on any page to see the exact before/after JSON-LD.</li>
        <li><strong>Apply</strong> — check the acknowledgement box and click Apply. Nothing is written to WordPress before this step.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="muted">The page list stays visible below the wizard at every step, and the step indicator lets you jump back to any step you've already completed.</p>

      <h3>4. After applying</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Verify live pages</strong> — re-checks the actual public page for the JSON-LD.</li>
        <li><strong>Undo last change</strong> — restores the previous state, including the original Rank Math output, for selected pages.</li>
        <li><strong>Run history</strong> — keeps every past run for the site so you can revisit it.</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="dialog-actions"><button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" id="close-help-footer">Got it</button></div>
    </div>
  </dialog>

  <main class="main">
    <div class="container">
